995	/**
996	 * Pick the best Proxmox node for a new server of `planRamMB`, when the
997	 * customer didn't choose a location explicitly. Bin-packs onto whichever
998	 * ONLINE, enabled node has the most free RAM after projecting this VM onto
999	 * it, staying under the CRITICAL threshold when any node can (falling back to
1000	 * least-bad if every node is already critical).
1001	 *
1002	 * THIRD copy, consolidated here. This existed as two near-identical private
1003	 * copies — `lib/order.ts` (VPS orders) and `lib/actions-nxcloud.ts` (NxCloud
1004	 * orders) — and `lib/game-order.ts`'s game-server order path never called
1005	 * either one at all: it creates its `Server` row with no `nodeId`, so every
1006	 * game server ever ordered falls through `worker/index.ts`'s `nodeFor()`
1007	 * fallback (`server.node ?? primary node`) and lands on the PRIMARY node
1008	 * regardless of its actual load. Confirmed live: `primary` sits at 84% real
1009	 * RAM and 200% committed CPU while other nodes are comparatively idle, and
1010	 * every game server in production has `nodeId: null`. Fixed by giving
1011	 * `game-order.ts` the same real scheduler VPS/NxCloud orders already use,
