188	 * `fulfilExternalPayment` (PayPal / Coinbase Commerce, below) can drive the exact
189	 * same claim/credit/provision/settle/notify logic from a SYNTHETIC session-shaped
190	 * object instead of a real Stripe retrieve. Nothing in this function's body
191	 * changed from the original `fulfilCheckoutSession` other than: (a) `sessionId` is
192	 * now read off `session.id` instead of being a separate parameter, and (b) the two
193	 * spots that are genuinely Stripe-only — crediting the wallet, and recording the
194	 * card for renewals — are gated on `provider === "stripe"`. Every claim/settle/
195	 * notify/provisioning line is untouched.
