347	// ===========================================================================
348	// History layer: HealthSample snapshots, uptime math, and StatusIncident state
349	//
350	// The four probes above are INSTANTANEOUS — they say what is true right now and
351	// keep no memory. Everything below turns that into history: the worker monitor
352	// calls sampleHealth() on its cadence to persist one HealthSample per component,
353	// and the readers compute uptime %, a bucketed timeline, and open/resolved
354	// incidents from those rows. All the arithmetic is factored into PURE functions
355	// (uptimeFromSamples / bucketTimeline / decideIncident) so it is unit-testable
356	// with an injected clock and injected samples, no DB required.
