726	/**
727	 * Data layer for the platform-wide Live Ops monitor (/admin/monitor).
728	 *
729	 * This is a v1 built entirely on data the platform ALREADY collects — it adds
730	 * no new sampling, no new schema. Three real sources are fused into one feed:
731	 *
732	 *   1. Node utilization (`lib/node-capacity.ts` allNodeUtil) — CPU/RAM/DISK for
733	 *      Proxmox compute nodes, ACCOUNTS/DISK for hosting nodes. CPU/RAM are
734	 *      queried LIVE from Proxmox on every call (no caching) — this is the one
735	 *      genuinely real-time number in the feed. DISK is the pool's live status
736	 *      too. This is the exact function that already powers the node-capacity
737	 *      warning banner and the Nodes admin page.
738	 *   2. Recent actions — the `Job` table (every VPS + game-server provisioning/
739	 *      power/backup/etc. action) fused with `HostingTask` (the equivalent queue
740	 *      for shared-hosting accounts, which do NOT create Job rows — see
741	 *      worker/hosting.ts). Together these cover every server kind the platform
742	 *      runs. Zero new instrumentation: both tables are written by the existing
743	 *      action/worker code on every real operation.
744	 *   3. Per-server resource state — `Server.bwInBytes/bwOutBytes` (metered by
745	 *      lib/bandwidth.ts on the worker's 10-minute sweep), the latest
746	 *      `ServerDiskSample` row (same sweep, guest-agent disk usage), and for
747	 *      shared hosting `HostingAccount.diskUsedMB`/`serveHttpOk`/`serveHttpsOk`
748	 *      (hostingUsageSweep / hostingHealthSweep). These are real but NOT
749	 *      per-request-live — they refresh on the worker's cadence (~10 min) and
750	 *      each row's own timestamp is returned so the UI can say exactly how
751	 *      stale it is instead of implying it's instantaneous.
752	 *
753	 * WHAT THIS DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO: there is no live per-VM CPU/RAM series
754	 * (Proxmox reports that per-VM, but nothing persists it, and polling every VM's
755	 * `/qemu/{vmid}/status/current` on every fleet-wide poll would multiply load on
756	 * Proxmox by the server count for every admin with this tab open) and there is
757	 * no live connection/session count anywhere on the platform (RCON can fetch a
758	 * Minecraft server's online-player count, but only one server at a time, on
759	 * demand — there is no fleet-wide sweep that samples it). Both are real v2
760	 * candidates, not faked here. See the doc comment on `MonitorFeed.gaps`.
761	 */
762	import { db } from "./db";
