277	/**
278	 * Shared per-server DISK EXPANSION core — the money path for growing a single
279	 * server's OWN root disk without touching its plan's CPU/RAM/price.
280	 *
281	 * Used by the wallet flow (lib/actions-disk.ts expandServerDisk) and by the
282	 * Stripe confirm route so a paid checkout can apply the expansion immediately.
283	 * Plain server module (NOT "use server") — same shape as lib/resize.ts, and it
284	 * deliberately mirrors that file line-for-line so the two money paths can never
285	 * drift apart.
286	 *
287	 * ─── GROWTH IS ONE-WAY ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
288	 * There is no shrink counterpart to `applyDiskExpand`, and nothing here (or
289	 * anywhere else) ever decrements `Server.extraDiskGB`.
290	 *
291	 * ─── WHY THIS CANNOT DOUBLE-CHARGE ──────────────────────────────────────────
292	 *  1. `diskExpandQuote` is the ONLY place the prorated amount is computed, and
293	 *     both the wallet path and the Stripe-confirm path call it.
294	 *  2. The wallet is debited exactly once, inside the same $transaction that
295	 *     creates the DISK_EXPAND job — a rolled-back debit leaves no job, and a
296	 *     job that exists was always paid for.
297	 *  3. On the card path the wallet is NOT touched until Stripe clears: checkout
298	 *     charges only the card remainder, the confirm route credits that remainder
299	 *     to the wallet and then debits the FULL proration, so the two net out.
300	 *  4. `creditCheckoutSession`'s UNIQUE(stripeSessionId) makes the confirm route
301	 *     idempotent — a reloaded/replayed confirm URL credits (and therefore
302	 *     applies) nothing a second time.
303	 *  5. `Server.extraDiskGB` is advanced by the WORKER on success, never here, so
304	 *     a failed expansion is refunded by the worker's reconcile pass and the
305	 *     customer never renews on storage they didn't get.
306	 */
