845	 * Create ONE real `Plan` row for this exact spec — the same manual-accommodation
846	 * pattern already proven in production once (see the sort-order doc comment
847	 * above), now automated. Re-validates guardrails AND capacity from scratch (a
848	 * client-supplied price/spec is never trusted for money — mirrors every other
849	 * quote→place split in this codebase) before writing anything.
850	 *
851	 * Created INACTIVE with `sortOrder: 999` so it NEVER appears in any catalog query
852	 * (every page that lists plans filters `active: true` — see
853	 * app/dashboard/deploy/page.tsx) — it exists solely to be the ONE plan this ONE
854	 * order's Server row points at. From here on, every downstream money path
855	 * (lib/order.ts orderQuote/placeOrder, lib/resize.ts, lib/renewal-charge.ts,
856	 * lib/capacity.ts, admin displays) reads straight off the `Plan` relation exactly
857	 * like it does for a premade plan — no special-casing needed anywhere else.
