941	// Pure pricing + guardrail math for CUSTOM VPS / game-server specs — servers
942	// bigger than the biggest premade plan ("Max"). No DB, no server-only imports:
943	// this is the ONE formula shared by the client-side deploy wizards (instant price
944	// as a slider moves, no round trip) and the server-side quote/order path
945	// (lib/custom-plan.ts, which re-validates everything here before a Plan row is
946	// ever created — a client-computed price is never trusted for money).
947	//
948	// ─── WHY "CUSTOM" EXISTS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
949	// The premade ladder tops out at Max (4 vCPU / 16 GB / 120 GB). A customer who
950	// needs more than that on ANY dimension gets a one-off Plan row sized exactly to
951	// what they asked for (see lib/custom-plan.ts createCustomPlan) instead of being
952	// turned away or overpaying for a fixed "XL" tier that's still too small. So a
953	// valid custom spec is, by definition, Max-or-bigger on every dimension and
954	// STRICTLY bigger on at least one — never a way to buy something Max-sized (or
955	// smaller) at a different price, which would undercut the catalog and break the
956	// price-monotonic / disk-monotonic invariants lib/resize.ts depends on to keep
957	// upgrades honest.
958	//
959	// ─── PRICING FORMULA DERIVATION ──────────────────────────────────────────────
960	// The live ladder (prisma — Plan table) and its price DELTAS between adjacent
961	// tiers:
962	//
963	//   Tier      vCPU  RAM(GB)  Disk(GB)  Price      Δ vCPU  Δ RAM  Δ Disk  Δ Price
964	//   Starter     1      2        25     $8.88
965	//   Standard    2      4        50    $12.99        1       2      25    411¢
966	//   Pro         3      8        80    $20.99        1       4      30    800¢
967	//   Max         4     16       120    $32.99        1       8      40   1200¢
968	//
969	// A pure 3-variable linear fit (price = a·Δvcpu + b·Δram_GB + c·Δdisk_GB) across
970	// those three deltas turns out to be OVER-determined in a way the real ladder
971	// can't satisfy exactly: solving any two of the three delta-equations for
972	// (a, b, c) and checking against the third leaves a residual (405¢ vs 800¢ i.e
973	// disk-GB deltas here are exactly `20*Δvcpu + 2.5*Δram_GB`, so the three price
974	// points don't sit on a single consistent (a,b,c) — there's no clean 3-variable
975	// exact solution, only a best fit). So rather than force an unstable joint
976	// regression across three highly-correlated columns (cpu/ram/disk all grow
977	// together tier-to-tier), we ANCHOR the disk rate to a number the platform
978	// already charges for exactly this resource — `extra_disk_gb_price_cents`
979	// (lib/disk-expand.ts / lib/settings.ts), the live $0.10/GB/month a customer on
980	// ANY premade plan already pays to add root disk beyond their plan's included
981	// amount. Reusing it here means a GB of disk costs the same $ whether it comes
982	// from the extra-disk upsell or from building a custom plan — one number, one
983	// meaning, platform-wide.
984	//
985	// With disk fixed at that rate (10¢/GB), each tier-to-tier price delta minus its
986	// disk contribution attributes the REMAINDER to cpu + ram:
987	//
988	//   Standard-Starter: 411 - 10·25 = 161 = 1a + 2b
989	//   Pro-Standard:      800 - 10·30 = 500 = 1a + 4b
990	//   Max-Pro:          1200 - 10·40 = 800 = 1a + 8b
991	//
992	// Least-squares fit of those three (a, b) equations (normal equations
993	// 3a+14b=1461, 14a+84b=8722) solves EXACTLY to a = 11, b = 102 — i.e. $0.11 per
994	// extra vCPU/month and $1.02 per extra GB RAM/month. (RAM dominates the ladder's
995	// price growth far more than CPU does, which matches lib/capacity.ts's own
996	// framing of RAM as "the scarce resource" the platform oversells carefully
997	// while CPU is comparatively cheap to add.)
998	//
999	// All three rates are admin-tunable via lib/settings.ts (`custom_plan_per_vcpu_cents`,
1000	// `custom_plan_per_ram_gb_cents`; disk reuses the existing `extra_disk_gb_price_cents`)
1001	// so the catalog can be retuned without a redeploy if the premade ladder ever moves.
1002	export const CUSTOM_PLAN_DEFAULT_RATES: CustomPlanRates = {
1003	  perVcpuCents: 11,
1004	  perRamGbCents: 102,
1005	  perDiskGbCents: 10, // mirrors extra_disk_gb_price_cents's shipped default
1006	};
